---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ReviewsRail from '../../components/ReviewsRail.astro';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://ka-performancefl.com/locations/gainesville/';

// Home > Gainesville. There is deliberately no /locations/ index page, so the
// trail skips straight from the root to this page rather than inventing a
// middle crumb that would 404 the moment anyone clicked it.
const breadcrumb = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://ka-performancefl.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Gainesville', item: PAGE_URL },
  ],
};

const services = [
  {
    href: '/services/web-design/',
    kicker: 'Web design',
    blurb: 'Designed from a blank page for your business, not chosen from a theme shop.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/ai-integration/',
    kicker: 'AI integration',
    blurb: 'Assistants that answer visitors at 11pm and automations that give hours back.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/seo-ai-search/',
    kicker: 'SEO & AI search',
    blurb: 'The local half of search, done properly, plus an honest list for the rest.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/accessibility/',
    kicker: 'Accessibility',
    blurb: 'Measured against WCAG 2.2 AA before launch. Existing sites get audited.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Web Design in Gainesville, FL | K & A Performance"
  description="Web design and AI integration from a Gainesville studio. Two founders, no account managers, in-person meetings if you want them, and quotes are always free."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumb)} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-40 pb-16 md:pt-48">
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-muted">
      Gainesville, Florida
    </p>
    <h1 data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mt-6 font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,6vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.04]">
      Web design in Gainesville, <span class="text-accent">from two people who live here</span>
    </h1>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This is the home market, not a city name rented for a landing page. K
      &amp; A Performance is based in Gainesville, the work is done in
      Gainesville, and if you want the first conversation to happen across a
      table instead of over email, that is a short drive rather than a flight.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Who you are actually hiring</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Two people, and you will deal with both of them. Alex Anderson does the
      design and the development, so whoever drew your layout is also the one
      writing the code, and nothing gets mistranslated in a handoff between
      departments that do not exist. Kristina Anderson runs strategy and
      content, which in practice means she is the one asking why a page exists
      at all and what it is supposed to make somebody do once they are on it.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      There is no account manager in the middle, no ticket queue, and nobody
      junior quietly doing the work at midnight. The trade is that we take on
      fewer projects than an agency would. The upside is that the people who
      pitched you are the people who build it, and they are still answering the
      email a year later.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Meeting in person is on the table</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Most of the work runs over email, shared links, and a staging site you can
      open whenever you like, and plenty of clients never want more than that.
      But a first meeting in a room is genuinely faster for some businesses.
      Watching an owner describe their busiest hour, or point at the one thing
      on their current site that makes the phone ring, tells us more in twenty
      minutes than a questionnaire does in a week. If that sounds like you, say
      so and we will come to you.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      It also means the site does not disappear into an inbox after launch. When
      something needs changing before an event, a season, or a grant deadline,
      you are asking a neighbour rather than opening a support case.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">The towns we count as neighbours</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Alachua, Newberry, High Springs and Ocala are close enough that we treat
      them exactly like Gainesville: same in-person option, same response times,
      same pricing. Small towns tend to get the worst of the web industry. A
      site a relative built years ago and cannot update, or a monthly platform
      fee paid forever for the privilege of not being allowed to edit your own
      opening hours. Both are fixable, and neither requires you to be inside the
      city limits to get help with it.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Gainesville is still winnable</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This is a market where good work still shows. Plenty of businesses here
      have no site worth the name, and plenty more have one nobody has opened on
      a phone since it launched. Ranking for a search with Gainesville attached
      comes down to a Google Business Profile that matches your site exactly,
      pages that say something true and specific about what you do here, and
      reviews from people who really came in. We do the on-site half properly
      and hand you a short, honest list for the rest, because the parts we
      cannot do for you are the parts that move the map.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      And if what you actually want is AI working inside the business rather
      than a new site, that exists too:
      <a href="/ai-launch/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">the 90-Day AI Launch</a>
      is twelve weekly working sessions with a Gainesville developer, ending
      with a real workflow running in your own accounts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">What we build here</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Every project starts with the same question: what does this site have to
      do, and what is stopping it. From there it is usually some mix of these
      four.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The proof is already around town.
      <a href="https://projectmakeover.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">Project Makeover</a>,
      the nonprofit based out of the University of Florida that remakes a
      school in a single weekend, runs on a site we built. So does the
      Florida Disability Access and Awareness Foundation, a Gainesville
      nonprofit, and so does Dancing Crafter. The studio itself is
      Gainesville, and so is a good share of the work.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {services.map((s) => (
        <a href={s.href} data-animate="frame-lift" class="glow-frame group flex flex-col p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-accent">{s.kicker}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">{s.blurb}</p>
          <p class="mt-5 font-heading text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent">
            Read more <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-10 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Building in Jacksonville or further up the coast instead? That runs
      remote, and it is described on the
      <a href="/locations/jacksonville/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">Jacksonville page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="border-t border-ink/10">
    <ReviewsRail />
  </div>

  <section class="px-6 pb-40 pt-16 md:pt-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
      <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,5.5vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.05]">
        Let's talk about it <span class="text-accent">locally</span>
      </p>
      <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Tell us what the site has to do and we will tell you what it would take,
        what it would cost, and whether it is worth doing at all. Coffee
        optional. The quote is free either way.
      </p>
      <div data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-10">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-accent">Start a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
